// boxcxx — <__bits/version_type_traits>
//
// The feature-test macros [version.syn] owned by <type_traits>.
//
// __cpp_lib_reference_from_temporary mirrors <type_traits>'s own
// __has_builtin guard: both traits it names are compiler-builtin-backed
// with no library fallback, so the macro must appear exactly when they do.
//
// transformation_trait_aliases needed aligned_storage_t and
// aligned_union_t -- deprecated in C++23 and still required by it.
//
// is_layout_compatible and is_pointer_interconvertible are each one trait
// plus one [meta.member] FUNCTION; the function half was the missing half
// of both, and neither macro is guarded on __has_builtin because
// <type_traits> already names the underlying builtins unconditionally --
// a toolchain without them cannot compile the header at all, so a guard
// here would only pretend to be portable.
//
// Deliberately absent (see <version>'s list): is_implicit_lifetime,
// result_of_sfinae.
//
// Every block below is gated on BOXCXX_OWNS_<stem>, and this file has NO
// include guard: it is meant to be included once per owning header, each time
// defining only what that header declared it owns. [support.limits.general]
// says a macro is defined by <version> AND by the header that provides the
// feature; it does not say every header that happens to include this leaf.
// A header that answers for a feature it does not provide is answering a
// question it was not asked, so it no longer does. <version> defines
// BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL and takes the lot. Checked by tools/cxx_ftm_audit.sh.

